-- title:
--   Ogg's unit and the two minimal primes over p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ jq$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $p$. Assume `hmem`: the Laurent series $\mathrm{modularUnitSeries}\ p = \Delta \cdot (\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ p\ \Delta)^{-1}$ lies in $F$, where $\Delta$ is the series $q$ times the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ` over $\mathbb{Q}$. Write $A =$ `HpoolLevelRing.Afin p` for the $j$-finite chart $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ℤ F (IgusaScheme.jFull p)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) of $F$ attached to the element $j \in F$ given by the $q$-expansion of the $j$-function. The assertion is that there exist elements $u, v \in A$ and ideals $P_0, P_1$ of $A$ such that, in $F$, $u$ equals the element $\langle \mathrm{modularUnitSeries}\ p, \mathtt{hmem}\rangle$ and $v$ equals $p^{12}$ times its inverse; $P_0$ and $P_1$ are prime and distinct; the set of minimal primes of the ideal of $A$ generated by $p$ is exactly $\{P_0, P_1\}$; and $u \notin P_0$, $u \in P_1$, $v \in P_0$, $v \notin P_1$.
--
--   This records the arithmetic of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ on the integral model of $X_0(p)$: its special fibre at $p$ has exactly two irreducible components, the unit being invertible along one and vanishing along the other, while its Fricke transform $p^{12}u^{-1}$ behaves the other way round. It is used by the construction of coordinates on the two-chart integral model, in the lemmas [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_coordinate_forall_mem_range_compInf_and_not_mem_range_compZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_coordinate_forall_mem_range_compInf_and_not_mem_range_compZero) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_equiv_pullback_compInf_compZero_ssJSet_germ_jCoordBC_sub_constSection_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_equiv_pullback_compInf_compZero_ssJSet_germ_jCoordBC_sub_constSection_mem).
